810509efe134bcc","job_sha256":"e884fd2027c4b3b09ebc0258d3640fad76263912559b5dd774113eb4ebda2733","passed":true,"runtime":{"available_cpus":32,"machine":"yotko-evo-x2","numpy":"2.4.4","platform":"Linux-7.0.0-34-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.39","python":"3.13.12","threads_configured":1,"threads_verified":[{"effective":1,"library":"libscipy_openblas64_-32a4b2a6.so"}]},"source_output_sha256":"285c6f4ff02cae325a59ed6e61a033a5ec0d9782092f76596fa4daaad8cb0fdc"},{"after_sha256":"b9436bf3ec7100f7b70698ef7740de17780f0d3b155a5aa42a733402f4e0c70e","before_sha256":"b9436bf3ec7100f7b70698ef7740de17780f0d3b155a5aa42a733402f4e0c70e","job_id":"a13_validate_plain_ext_cd4ffbca1a2b1d99b5ff9058","job_sha256":"ff1ddf33b990b8b77d60eea5bd663ad6a7177ac923679a75203aa33da7b06e77","passed":true,"runtime":{"available_cpus":32,"machine":"yotko-evo-x2","numpy":"2.4.4","platform":"Linux-7.0.0-34-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.39","python":"3.13.12","threads_configured":1,"threads_verified":[{"effective":1,"library":"libscipy_openblas64_-32a4b2a6.so"}]},"source_output_sha256":"d66abbf4c14cc0ba315ab445bb4afc4c9f017acefff0807651bf41415268d4aa"}],"reasons":{"v3/admission_a13.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): binding() and verify() accept the new admission scope 'A10_nominal_after_A14' beside the two A13 scopes. Every Part 2 condition is unchanged: the floor(N/1000) cap, one admitted row per context, the balanced-witness exclusion, the item 12(b) screens and the re-test violation refusal. Only the A14 publication writes that scope. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds.","v3/artifacts.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): adds A14_COMMIT 17f17ef9. Current (non-historical) A10 launches and publications verify strictly against 17f17ef9, whose design note must contain the A13 clarification and '### Amendment A14' and match the working note byte for byte; plans pinned to 48815a65 or earlier, including A13's, verify historically by ancestry and committed bytes. Digest, seal, canonical JSON, seed and job-identity functions are unchanged. A2 re-pinned (68c30205 to cb526190, recorded under a14). Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the current-pin change.","v3/compatibility_a10.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): _execute_proof routes a selected a13_validate_plain_ext job that carries an a13_replay binding to replay_a14.replay, the isolated re-simulation of every recorded replicate from its seed in an empty scratch root with each checkpoint compared; collect_record attaches that binding (plan, job, recorded result, checkpoint documents) to selected A13-phase jobs and, for the sealed single-host registered A13 plan, takes the scheduling class from the hash-bound original validation plan (worker_seconds x R_max/3); build_record passes the proof sources' declared historical roots to the single-host preflight. Population, stratum, selection, comparison bytes, before/after hashes, record fields and approval are unchanged, and ordinary execution cannot reach the replay path. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (the authorized compatibility-replay adapter); A14 stated exception: the snapshot-path repair (declared roots).","v3/compatibility_shards_a11.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): source_historical_roots() unions each proof source's declared absolute historical_roots with any roots frozen in its spec; portable_inventory() refuses a proof input outside the checkout or those roots before staging and seals the roots and their hash into the inventory; stage_inputs() re-verifies that scope; qualification_bundle(), freeze() and single_preflight() carry the same roots, so qualification and the proof use identical declarations. Selection, comparison, scheduling, the identity-pair reservation and finality are unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the snapshot-path repair.","v3/forecast_a14.py":"New A14 module (item 6): stages a read-only 55817036 source view from git blobs; validates the sealed forecast configuration (interpreter, Python and numpy versions, package paths outside the checkout); runs the three hash-pinned assessment scripts unchanged in an isolated -I -B interpreter with repository-import and data-path guards and inventory-mapped reads; returns only the two round-2 probabilities with environment and hash records (exit 78 is a finding). Used only by A14 preparation and preentry; no estimation, validation or proof path imports it. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds.","v3/history_a14.py":"New A14 module (item 1): the roles-based sealed history inventory builder (read-only, hash-verified copies with aliases) and the read-only verifier, which recomputes A13 eligibility and classifications from the copies and checks the A13 round, the original refusal and the committed compatibility records; it writes nothing on failure. Used only by A14 preparation and preentry. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds.","v3/host_a11.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): execute_scratch() gains an a14_validate_plain_ext2 branch with its own checkpoint context and a round-2 scientific-halt marker; run_host() transfers that kind's durable replicate checkpoints (a14_checkpoint) and reports a14_halt for it. A13 and every other kind follow their existing paths unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (dispatch).","v3/multihost_a11.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): ALLOWED_KINDS adds a14_validate_plain_ext2; freeze() refuses registered A14 (single-host only) and gives the kind the R_max/3 ordering weight; prepare() binds the A14 round; the coordinator latches A14 halts, hands out A14 durable checkpoints in claims, accepts a14_checkpoint and a14_halt (added to the RPC allowlist) and latches nondeterminism for that kind. Snapshot-path repair: freeze() accepts --historical-root (or the spec's declared roots) and seals the roots and their hash into pull_dispatch, validate_extension() checks them, and the coordinator's phase snapshots use them. Claims, comparisons and checks for other kinds are unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (dispatch); A14 stated exception: the snapshot-path repair.","v3/production_runner.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): execute() dispatches a14_validate_plain_ext2 (non-registered only as a rehearsal or configuration test with non-reserved seeds); the a13_validate_plain_ext branch first routes an authorized replay (replay_a14.authorized_replay, true only inside the proof adapter's context for that job and scratch root) to execute_replay; worker() and the nondeterminism check latch the A14 round; validate_spec() verifies A14 specs inside their declared execution inputs; a guard rejects the A14 reserved range [2^61, 2^62) for every non-A14 job; launch() binds the A14 round, refuses a latched A14 halt, and memory-manages and rechecks the A14 phase; calibration loading covers the new kind. A2 re-pinned (e9fe15b9 to 0d3f5f3c, recorded under a14). The scientific execute paths of existing kinds, outputs, completion and checkpoint writes are unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (dispatch, the replay adapter, and the A14 reserved-range guard, which no existing job seed meets).","v3/qualification_a11.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): a14_validate_plain_ext2 qualifies from non-registered short fixture streams (seeds at or above 2^128), as A13 does; build() passes the spec's declared historical roots to the inventory, copies each bundle file from its verified source with hash checks before and after copying, and makes external or aliased copies read-only. The X2-1 reference rule, the comparison and the evidence fields used for approval are unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds; A14 stated exception: the snapshot-path repair.","v3/replay_a14.py":"New A14 module, the compatibility-replay adapter (step 2): binds an A13 plan job, its recorded result and checkpoint documents; is authorized only inside the proof's producer context for that job and an empty scratch root; re-simulates each recorded replicate from its seed with A13's unchanged extension_stage and requires byte-identical checkpoints. It never resumes the A13 root, loads a checkpoint as completed work, derives a statistic, or writes a family record. It is the only exception to the reserved-seed guard, limited to the A13 plan's own jobs and seeds. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (the authorized proof adapter; unreachable from ordinary execution).","v3/snapshot_a11.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): dependencies() takes A14 phase inputs only from each job's declared hash-verified copies; normalize_historical_roots(), historical_roots() and verify_historical_scope() bound external inputs and aliases to explicitly declared, hashed absolute roots; inventory() keeps the exact pre-A14 row layout and bytes for in-checkout inputs, stages external inputs at v3/historical_inputs/<digest>/<name> with source and aliases, and refuses undeclared roots and destination collisions; fetch() and receive() re-verify scope, and receive() rejects conflicting aliases and protects declared roots. The step 3 rehearsal confirmed unchanged in-checkout staging at both identities and the external branch on two hosts. Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the snapshot-path repair.","v3/table_compatibility_A2.json":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): a new a14 entry re-pins exactly artifacts.py (68c30205 to cb526190) and production_runner.py (e9fe15b9 to 0d3f5f3c), with their previous hashes, design commit 17f17ef9 and dated reasons; approved_boundary_sha256 changes for those two only, and every other pinned dependency stays exact. Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the current-pin change (its A2 re-pin record; the production_runner re-pin records the A14-only branch).","v3/table_labels_a5.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): assert_a5_seeds() forbids the widened reserved range [2^60, 2^62), covering both extension rounds (A5's existing reader already forbids both manifests through the receipt's union extension_seed_manifest); registered publication decides strict versus historical pin verification by A14_COMMIT. No existing A5 seed lies in the added range. The label job build, seeds, stage and classification are unchanged. Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the current-pin change (selection site); A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (the widened reserved-range seed guard; no existing A5 seed lies in it).","v3/table_validation_a4.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): selection sites only: publish() decides strict versus historical verification by A14_COMMIT, and prospective A13 admission applies to plans pinned to 48815a65 or 17f17ef9, so A14-pinned later validation families keep A13 Part 2's binding. No fit, validation, census or estimation function changes. Classification of the A14 change: A14 stated exception: the current-pin change (selection sites).","v3/validation_extension_a14.py":"New A14 module: the second and final extension round - invocation validation and the preliminary reservation, historical verification, eligibility, constants, pricing and the R_max floor of 24, the seed manifest in [2^61, 2^61 + 2^60) with its collision check, ordered replicates from 20 with durable checkpoints, the first-N* test on this round's data alone, the halt latch, decline, preentry, two-round reassembly and publication with both round bindings. It reuses A13's unchanged numerical stage, sample-size expression and test, and is not part of any completed estimation, validation or A13 computation. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds.","v3/worker_control.py":"A14 revision (8b176c73, identity 174ab660; the A14 build and its three review-fix rounds): arithmetic_class() and configuration_resources() recognize the v3-A14-extension-1 schema and a14_ kinds for memory classification, exactly as for A13. No job, seed, setting, result, selection or comparison is read or changed. Classification of the A14 change: A14-only branch, inert for earlier kinds (memory classification of the new schema; executor, scheduling or dispatch only)."},"schema":"v3-A11-compatibility-1","selection_rule":"two smallest digest([\"A11-compatibility\", phase, job_id]) per capability/setting"},"sha256":"36ec606a36e2f2aeeb7ef6eb383620797690ead41880057519f1a26e2a6cda04"}
